Z||000000||Posthumane||12-17-2001||05:24 PM||||Well, I busted part of my air dam off on my 84 SE while at a rally cross, which now gives me an excuse to get a new one. I was thinking of making a custom one out of fiberglass, but I also like the IMSA style aero kit on Hartz's 85 turbo. Where can I get this kind of kit, how much does it cost, and would it be worth my time to try and make one myself (not much exp w/ fiberglass yet).||||reg||1
Z||000001||Hartz||12-17-2001||08:49 PM||||Thanks.<P>The bad news:  I bought that body kit back in 1985 directly from DGP.  DGP, as a company, is no longer in business.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>The possible glimer of hope:  I've heard that IRM picked up all of the IMSA pieces.  Good luck trying to contact them, but since the front spoiler is common across both the wide body and Stage 1 kits, it should work.  I think there was one other place somewhere on the web that might have had IMSA pieces, but darned if I remember where it was.  Perhaps try searching the archives for the word "IMSA?"  <P>Best of luck,<BR>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>hartzfeld.home.mindspring.com||||reg||1
